scope: |
  SSC3-J4's last shape, `(bin cmp)` + `(brif)`, fused as a PEEPHOLE in `Exec.exec` rather
  than as a new opcode or a private flat encoding. §10.2 offered only those two because it
  assumed a fused operation must be represented; `exec` already holds a cursor, so the pair
  is `rest.head` / `rest.tail.head` and after J4b it is canonical and adjacent. IR, verifier,
  text form, round-trip gate, BridgeV2 and the charter are all untouched.

  WIDENED to v3/src/Main.scala for the OFF arm alone: `--no-fuse-cmpbr`, wired exactly like
  `--no-tag-cache` and `--no-prepare-cache` beside it, so both arms live in ONE binary and an
  A/B cannot accidentally compare two builds.
next: wire the OFF arm, then --sizes and PrintInlining before any clock
